\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Uniform remeshing. (a, b) The aneurysm sac before and after remeshing: the triangle size becomes uniform (edge-length CV 0.25 $\rightarrow $ 0.12, shortest edge 2\,$\mu $m $\rightarrow $ 24\,$\mu $m) while the shape and texture of the wall are preserved. (c, d) An opening before and after, seen obliquely from outside the vessel: the uneven rim is replaced by a planar pipe-section cut perpendicular to the centreline.}}{12}{figure.caption.13}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:dp_remesh}{{6}{12}{Uniform remeshing. (a, b) The aneurysm sac before and after remeshing: the triangle size becomes uniform (edge-length CV 0.25 $\rightarrow $ 0.12, shortest edge 2\,$\mu $m $\rightarrow $ 24\,$\mu $m) while the shape and texture of the wall are preserved. (c, d) An opening before and after, seen obliquely from outside the vessel: the uneven rim is replaced by a planar pipe-section cut perpendicular to the centreline}{figure.caption.13}{}}
